# Virtual environment

This repository uses a local virtual environment at `.venv`.

- Before running **any** `python`, `pip`, `uv`, `pytest`, or package CLIs (`methyl-*`, etc.) in the terminal, activate it from the repo root:

  `source .venv/bin/activate`

- Prefer one-shot form when scripting commands: `source .venv/bin/activate && python -m pytest ...`

- Do not assume system Python has project dependencies; tests and imports should be validated inside `.venv`.
